---
description: Keep test expectations visible in test methods; do not hide expected objects behind helpers.
globs: src/**/*.test/**/*.cs,src/**/*.test.integration/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# Visible Test Expectations

When asserting outcomes, the reader must see the expected shape in the test method itself.

## Required

- Write the full expected object inline in `BeEquivalentTo`, `ContainExactlyEquivalent`, or equivalent assertions.
- Keep scenario literals inline (`"Process this request"`, `"lookup_item"`), not behind test-level constants or factory methods.
- Put equivalency exclusions in the same assertion when members are runtime-dependent.
- Use `Infrastructure/` helpers only for setup, normalization, deserialization, or shared assertion options — not for building the expected result object.
- Shared assertion option helpers are allowed when their summary documents every excluded field.

## Forbidden

- `CreateExpectedResult()`, `BuildExpected...()`, or similar helpers that hide the expected object from the test method.
- Do not assign the expected object to a local variable such as `var expected = ...` when it is only used by `BeEquivalentTo` or `ContainExactlyEquivalent`.
- Test-level constants whose only purpose is to hide readable scenario text or expected values.
- Property-by-property assertion chains when the whole result should be asserted with `BeEquivalentTo`.

## Good

```csharp
result.Should().BeEquivalentTo(
    new ProcessResult
    {
        Success = true,
        Summary = "Task completed successfully.",
        Steps =
        [
            new ProcessStep
            {
                Index = 0,
                Description = "Process this request",
                ActionName = "lookup_item",
                Input = new Dictionary<string, object?>(),
                Output = new LookupResult
                {
                    ItemName = "example"
                },
                Error = null,
                StartedAt = default,
                CompletedAt = default
            }
        ]
    },
    ProcessStepAssertionOptions.ExcludeDynamicValues );
```

`ExcludeDynamicValues` must document every excluded member in its summary, grouped by type:

- `ProcessStep`: `StartedAt`, `CompletedAt`
- `LookupResult`: `Timestamp`, `CorrelationId`

## Bad

```csharp
result.Should().BeEquivalentTo(
    ProcessExpectations.CreateExpectedResult(),
    ProcessStepAssertionOptions.ExcludeDynamicValues );

step.ActionName.Should().Be( "lookup_item" );
step.Description.Should().Be( "Process this request" );
```
